The problem was that the `pip` package files were missing from `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/` — only the `.dist-info` metadata directory remained, making it look like pip was installed when it actually wasn't.

I removed the orphaned `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` directory and re-ran `python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade`, which restored the full pip package. pip is now working:

```
pip 24.3.1 from /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip (python 3.13)
```

